<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Staraya Russa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Staraya Russa is a town in the Novgorod region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ilmen">Lake Ilmen</a>, first recorded in the eleventh century. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the second town of the Novgorod Republic and a centre of salt production. In 1456 the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow">Vasily II of Moscow</a> defeated the Novgorodians there, leading to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-yazhelbitsy">Treaty of Yazhelbitsy</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fyodor-dostoevsky">Fyodor Dostoevsky</a> later spent his summers in the town.</p></div>
